WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:10.600
Spectacular, isn't it?

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:11.440
Probably.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:12.700
What is it?

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.420
I've created a simulation of the entire universe.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.950
Oh, in that case, it stinks.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.610
I keep forgetting, Professor, are we in the entire universe?

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.370
Why, naturally.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:30.700
Good news everyone, we've got a delivery!

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.980
Woo hoo!

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.990
But first, role call.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:35.490
Leela.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:36.490
Here.

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:37.200
Fry.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.200
Present.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.360
Scruffy.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.360
Here.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:41.070
Hermes!

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.910
Check.

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:43.910
Bender!

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:45.250
Bite my shiny metal pixel.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.030
Amy.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.890
Schmallviously.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:48.760
And the rest.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:52.480
Yay, I'm an unnamed member of the group!

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.370
That's amazing, Professor.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.990
How'd you make it so crummy?

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:58.210
It wasn't easy. Even to achieve

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:06.160
this level of realism requires vast amounts of computing
power. My simpleton uses more electricity

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:12.070
than a hundred bug zappers. Which reminds me,
I had to unplug our bug zappers.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:16.570
Oh!

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:16.870
Got him!

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:19.570
The mosquito is still alive.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:20.530
There's a mosquito?

